Fictional EP Tracklist

Track 1: Locomotives Bruise the Winter Wheat
- Story & Context: Recorded during the blizzard that permanently severed rail transport between the Longyearbyen freight depot and the mountain intake tunnel, the track chronicles the night archivist Jérémie dropped an uncataloged flask of 19th-century Ukrainian rye seeds into the gears of an idling track-clearing engine. The resulting crunch was captured by a boundary microphone taped to the rail line, setting off an argument between the crew that ended with Vulpian singing a distorted cadence through the diesel exhaust. The cold was so severe that the bass guitar's low E-string snapped across his knuckle, leaving frozen rust and crimson on the pickup while he chanted, "Let the heavy iron chew what our mouths forgot."
