Track 2: "Was That the Last Car Out of Longyearbyen?"
- Story & Context: In this late-night bunker confession, sound programmer Hildur admits over a ticking 90-BPM zouk hi-hat to forging the cargo timetables so she could remain alone in the vault when the final civilian transport train departed Svalbard for the mainland. While she monitored the zinc humidity meters with shaking, nicotine-stained fingers, Vulpian improvised a suffocating, downward-sliding bassline underneath her taped micro-cassette diary. The sensory silence was broken only by the subterranean air scrubber groaning like a dying choir, punctuated by her murmured hook: "The schedule is burnt, but my hip still remembers the sway."
