Track 3: Mèsi Pou La Grèv (Terminal Spur)
- Story & Context: The EP concludes with the mythic folklore surrounding the three-week logistical strike at the harbor terminus, where warehousemen refused to haul seed containers into the permafrost until their dead were commemorated. Rather than riot, the workers huddled around a single outdoor kerosene heater, dancing an agonizingly slow, two-step zouk funeral shuffle across the frozen ballast stone while Manuel tapped out syncopated rimshots on frozen kerosene drums. As dawn failed to break, the strikers and archivists joined in a resonant drone that shook the terminal buffers, harmonizing the refrain: "Praise the stalled wheel, praise the seed that waits out the world."
